@flexiarg ways-of-working/records-carry-warrant
@title Nothing is accepted on say-so
@keywords way of working, invariant, cascade live
@audience agents, operators, institution designers
@tone normative
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-11-02 by claude-16; runs correct it
@provenance declared in futon3c/holes/excursions/ways-of-working.json (claude-2 with Joe, 2026-11-02)
@why [creativity-commons/distributed-monitoring creativity-commons/producers-can-modify-the-tests agent/evidence-over-assertion]

! conclusion: Every reviewed change carries a warrant whose shas match the diff; a run without one is the dirty tree, not a veto.

  + IF:
    An assertion severed from its derivation cannot be checked, learned from, or recovered.

  + HOWEVER:
    Agents report work done, and reports are cheap to write. Reviewing every report by rerunning it costs more than the work.

  + THEN:
    Every reviewed change carries a warrant whose shas match the diff; a run without one is the dirty tree, not a veto.

  + BECAUSE:
    A warrant with matching shas lets anyone check a run later, while a pasted count convinces nobody tomorrow. In one traced case, none of 12 live gaps closed with an independent record.

  + VALIDATION:
    Does a change in review carry a warrant whose shas match its diff?
